---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PlatformCards from "../components/PlatformCards.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<Layout title="Install" description="Build and run Tor Browser Installer from source.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Get started</span>
      <h1>Installation</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="max-width: 62ch;">
        There is no pre-built binary yet. For now, build it yourself from source. 
        It's beta software, and building from source is the most trustworthy way to run it.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px;">1. Clone the repository</h2>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/reality-prod/tbi-rust.git
cd tbi-rust</code></pre>

      <h2 style="margin-top:36px;">2. Install Rust</h2>
      <p>If you don't have the Rust toolchain, get it from <a href="https://rustup.rs/">rustup.rs</a>.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:36px;">3. Build and run</h2>
      <pre><code>cargo run --release</code></pre>
      <p>
        Rust compiles one binary per platform. The same source, built once per OS, 
        handles the correct release JSON, archive format, and install routine for that platform.
      </p>

      <div class="platform-instructions">
        <h3>Platform-specific notes</h3>
        <div class="platform-notes">
          <div class="platform-note">
            <div class="platform-note-header">
              <strong>macOS</strong>
            </div>
            <p>
              After building, you may see a security warning when trying to run the binary. 
              Run this command to allow it:
            </p>
            <pre><code>xattr -cr target/release/tor-browser-builder</code></pre>
            <p>This removes the quarantine flag that macOS adds to downloaded files.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="platform-note">
            <div class="platform-note-header">
              <strong>Windows</strong>
            </div>
            <p>
              Windows SmartScreen may block the executable since it's unsigned. 
              Click "More info" then "Run anyway" to proceed.
            </p>
            <p>
              If downloading from GitHub, Chrome/Edge may warn about the file. 
              Keep the file and click "Run anyway" when prompted.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="platform-note">
            <div class="platform-note-header">
              <strong>Linux</strong>
            </div>
            <p>
              No special steps needed. Just run the binary after building.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Per-platform defaults</span>
      <h2>Where it installs, and how it gets the permissions it needs.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="max-width: 62ch; margin-bottom: 32px;">
        Every location matches that OS's conventions. The same place Finder, your package 
        manager, or a typical installer would put things.
      </p>
      <PlatformCards />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Using the app</span>
      <h2>Once it's running</h2>
      <ol class="usage-list">
        <li><strong>Launch the installer</strong> &mdash; run the compiled binary.</li>
        <li><strong>Choose install location</strong> &mdash; pre-filled with the platform default, editable.</li>
        <li><strong>Pick scope</strong> &mdash; <em>Just me</em> (no special privileges) or <em>All users</em> (system-wide, needs password).</li>
        <li><strong>Click Download & Install</strong> &mdash; app shows version and URL, waits for confirmation, then downloads, verifies, installs.</li>
        <li><strong>Launch Tor Browser</strong> &mdash; directly from completion screen, or from the app's home screen next time.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Troubleshooting</span>
      <h2>Common issues</h2>
      <div class="trouble">
        <div>
          <h4><Icon name="cross" size={16} /> &ldquo;Could not fetch release information&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>Check your connection, or the Tor Project's release API may be down. Try again later.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4><Icon name="cross" size={16} /> &ldquo;Checksum mismatch&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>The download was corrupted or intercepted. The installer refuses to install it. Download again.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4><Icon name="cross" size={16} /> &ldquo;PGP signature verification failed&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>The signature doesn't match the Tor Browser Developers key. Installer refuses to install. Could indicate a compromised download.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4><Icon name="cross" size={16} /> Permission denied (macOS/Linux)</h4>
          <p>System-wide installs need your admin password for <code>sudo -s</code>. Used locally for that one command, never stored or transmitted.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:28px;">
        Click <strong>View commands</strong> inside the app at any time to see every system 
        command it has run, in order. Useful for debugging and for checking its work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 760px; }
  .usage-list { display: grid; gap: 14px; padding-left: 22px; }
  .usage-list li { color: var(--text); }
  .trouble { display: grid; gap: 24px; margin-top: 24px; }
  .trouble h4 { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; color: var(--app-error); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .trouble p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-muted); }

  .platform-instructions {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--app-purple-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--app-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  
  .platform-instructions h3 {
    color: var(--app-purple-deep);
    margin: 0 0 16px 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  
  .platform-notes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  
  .platform-note {
    padding: 16px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--app-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  
  .platform-note-header {
    color: var(--app-purple-deep);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  
  .platform-note p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 12px 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  
  .platform-note pre {
    background: var(--tor-grey);
    border: 1px solid var(--app-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    margin: 0 0 12px 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  
  .platform-note pre code {
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    color: var(--tor-dark-grey);
  }
</style>
